# Graph Link Prediction Project

## Overview
This project focuses on analyzing large graph datasets and performing link prediction using machine learning. The goal is to determine whether a connection (edge) between two nodes is likely to exist based on structural properties of the graph.

We use real-world datasets, extract graph-based features, and train a classification model to distinguish between existing and non-existing links.

```

## Datasets

The following datasets are used:

- CA-GrQc.txt (Directed co-authorship network)
- com-dblp.ungraph.txt (Undirected collaboration network)

### File Setup

If using Google Colab, update file paths:

```python
FILE1 = "/content/drive/MyDrive/.../CA-GrQc.txt"
